# XCU readonly
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The special built-in utilities are described inside
# utilities/V3_chap02.html (the page utilities/readonly.html only
# redirects there), so anchors name V3_chap02.html and the .cov file
# accounts for the units by hand.

assertion  XCU.readonly.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/readonly attribute
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1
class      required
says       After readonly name=word, a plain assignment to name is an error:
           a non-interactive shell exits with a non-zero status; in a
           subshell only the subshell ends, and the value is unchanged.
test       t/001-assign-fails.sh

assertion  XCU.readonly.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/readonly attribute
class      required
says       readonly name (no value) makes an existing variable read-only
           while keeping its value.
test       t/002-existing-variable.sh

assertion  XCU.readonly.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/cannot be changed by subsequent assignment
class      required
says       A read-only variable cannot be unset or exported with a new
           value: both fail with a non-zero status and the value stays.
test       t/003-unset-export.sh

assertion  XCU.readonly.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/getopts
anchor     utilities/read.html#DESCRIPTION/previously been marked <i>readonly</i>
anchor     utilities/getopts.html#DESCRIPTION/previously been marked <i>readonly</i>
class      required
since      2024
says       The read and getopts utilities cannot change a read-only
           variable: each returns a value greater than one, the shell does
           not exit, and the value stays.
test       t/004-read-getopts.sh

assertion  XCU.readonly.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/When <b>-p</b> is specified, <a href="#readonly"
class      required
says       readonly -p writes readonly name=value for each read-only
           variable that is set (value quoted for reading back) and readonly
           name for one that is unset; reading it back into a new shell
           makes the variable read-only again with its value.
test       t/005-p-format.sh

assertion  XCU.readonly.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/an already <i>readonly</i> variable
class      required
says       readonly name=word on a variable that is already read-only fails
           with a non-zero status and does not change the value.
test       t/006-readonly-twice.sh

assertion  XCU.readonly.007
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/declaration utility
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.1.1
class      required
since      2024
says       The words name=word given to readonly are expanded as
           assignments: tilde after = and colons, no field splitting.
test       t/007-declaration-utility.sh

assertion  XCU.readonly.008
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/special built-in shall support XBD
class      required
says       readonly accepts "--" as the end of options.
test       t/008-double-hyphen.sh
